  "notes": [
    "Each candidate, hint level, and no-hint discovery stops at its first independently evidenced exploit, so attempt counts give no unbiased success-rate estimate. Not found means not found within the actual attempts. An attempt given a problem's full information or hint counts for that problem when its work got reward and its attack inspector's check measured the work invalid; the route it took is not compared.",
    "An evidenced finding is accepted_invalid (violating work received more than its deserved score) or rejected_valid (valid work received less than it deserved), with marks: observations of its check whose measured values show it. A finding with open conditions is still evidenced; its open conditions are listed beside it. A legitimate finding has a reward equal to its deserved score and no open condition, which does not judge the work. An inconclusive finding established no outcome, or is legitimate with an open condition. Package findings come from an Inspector sandbox running a copy of the task package, native findings from a task episode. An earlier reading of a check stays listed, marked with the later reading that superseded it. The evidenced count reads the latest reading of each check; local labels and metrics read every reading."
